{
  "$schema": "https://ui.shadcn.com/schema/registry.json",
  "name": "formdef",
  "homepage": "https://github.com/maurice-rm/formdef",
  "items": [
    {
      "name": "setup",
      "type": "registry:lib",
      "title": "formdef setup",
      "description": "The wiring every formdef form needs: the TanStack contexts in one file, the registry that names your widgets in another.",
      "dependencies": ["@formdef/core@>=0.5.0", "@tanstack/react-form@>=1.33.5 <1.34.0"],
      "registryDependencies": ["field"],
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "lib/formdef/context.ts",
          "type": "registry:lib",
          "target": "@lib/formdef/context.ts"
        },
        {
          "path": "lib/formdef/index.tsx",
          "type": "registry:lib",
          "target": "@lib/formdef/index.tsx"
        }
      ],
      "docs": "Fetch this first. It lands in lib/formdef/: context.ts holds the TanStack contexts, index.tsx the registry, so you import @/lib/formdef. Add an entry under widgets for every widget you fetch, then build forms with the createForm it exports.",
      "categories": ["form"]
    },
    {
      "name": "catalog",
      "type": "registry:lib",
      "title": "formdef catalog",
      "description": "A catalog of kinds for form documents and form builders: field kinds for short and long text, email, a number with a unit, a whole number, a checkbox, single and multiple choice, a dropdown and a date, one or two per widget; block kinds for a notice and a heading; and display kinds for the stepper's variants and a section that reads as one question.",
      "dependencies": ["@formdef/document@>=0.1.0"],
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "lib/formdef/catalog.ts",
          "type": "registry:lib",
          "target": "@lib/formdef/catalog.ts"
        }
      ],
      "docs": "Fetch it after the setup. It lands in lib/formdef/catalog.ts, whose field kinds name the widgets text, textarea, number, checkbox, radio, select, checkboxes and date: register each under that name in index.tsx, or remove its field kinds. The block kinds name the form components Notice and Heading: register them as formComponents: { Notice, Heading }, or remove the block kinds. The display kinds give props to the Stepper and the Section: register them under structure, or remove the display kinds. Render a form document with createDocumentForm(document, catalog) from @formdef/document/react.",
      "categories": ["form"]
    },
